      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 5114298124278996232, guid: c800375dfcf2b054db4f0d8af5576733, type: 3}
      propertyPath: storyText
      value: "Ich lese in einem <i>biological survey</i> von 1988, vom <i>National
        Trust</i> in Auftrag gegeben:\r\n \r\np. 73\r\n7. Buildings\r\n7.2 Dovecote\r\n\r\nThe
        beetle fauna of the dovecote in the walled garden was investigated by Welch
        in 1983 (Welch, 1985) and a very interesting range of species found. Of greatest
        interest was the discovery of the nationally rare rove beetle <i>Phyllodrepa
        puberula</i>, a species only known from some 20 localities in Britain and
        not previously known in Norfolk. The species is believed to breed in bird
        nests. 35 individuals were found in dry dusty pigeon droppings from the roof
        of a store occupying half the ground floor of the dovecote.\r\n\r\n<u>Management
        Implications</u>\r\nAccumulations of nest litter and droppings should be
        permitted to remain in parts of the dovecote and not tidied up.\r\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 5114298124278996232, guid: c800375dfcf2b054db4f0d8af5576733, type: 3}
